Z||000000||ChadMan||07-03-2001||01:18 PM||||85 GT - 4 sp, 80K miles, PW, cruise, sunroof<P>Good:<BR>Motor sounds healthy, pulls strong & makes good oil pressure<BR>4-sp - shifts nice, clutch feels good<BR>Looks like it's never been wrecked - all panels line up & no visible frame damage<BR>Brakes are nice and firm - stops straight<BR>New cat and muffler<BR>Red paint needs buffed, but is NOT faded<BR>A/C works<BR>Good Firehawk tires<P>Bad:<BR>No wing!<BR>Ticking from firewall-side exhaust manifold<BR>Interior is trashed<BR>1/4 windows cracked<BR>Sunroof leaks<BR>Headliner replaced with some queer wetsuit material<BR>Neither headlight comes up (relay?)<P>Saw this for sale in Grandview yesterday...||||reg||5
Z||000001||DisfourDan||07-03-2001||01:38 PM||||Most of the problems with the Fiero can be fixed very easily.  If the VIN comes up clean, and the engine has no problems, Id say below 1600.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||07-03-2001||01:40 PM||||Hmmm ...<P>"No wing!" - personal preference but I think they look better without.  Of course, you could add one later.  Maybe trade Drew a wingless decklid for one of his winged ones.<P>"Ticking from firewall-side exhaust manifold" - something a few of us IndiOhio boys could correct in an afternoon.  Drew can drop a cradle is record time and we've got enough experience between him, William and Mike to make the job pretty easy.<P>"Interior is trashed" - a bargaining tool.  Use it to get a better price.<P>"1/4 windows cracked" - could probably find a set fairly cheap in the mall or contact Paul McKibben for a nice set.<P>"Sunroof leaks" - maybe something as simple as bad hinges.<P>"Headliner replaced with some queer wetsuit material" - if it's not dangling, don't worry about it unless it's some God-awful color.<P>"Neither headlight comes up (relay?)" - probably a question for Drew, William or Mike.  Use it as a bargaining tool to get the price down, then use the money saved to convert to the '87-'88 headlight system.<P>I'd pay $1500-$1700.  Mileage is good but it has some issues (one of which makes it "undriveable" at night).||||reg||6
